{title: 457 - I Love to Tell the Story}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #457 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 457}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]I love to tell the story
Of [C]unseen things a[G]bove,
Of [D]Jesus and His [G]glory,
Of Jesus and His [D]love.
I love to [D7]tell the [G]story,
Be[Em]cause I know ’tis [B]true;
It [C]satisfies my [G]longings
As [D7]nothing else can [G]do.
I [D]love to [D7]tell the [G]story,
’Twill [C]be my theme in [G]glory,
To tell the old, old [C]story
Of [G]Jesus [D7]and His [G]love.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[G]I love to tell the story,
[C]'twill be my [G]theme in glory,
[D]to tell the [G]old, old story
[D]of Jesus and his love.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]I love to tell the story;
[C]more wonderful [G]it seems
[D]than all [G]the golden fancies
[D]of all our golden dreams.
[D7]I love to [G]tell the story,
[Em]it did so [B]much for me;
[C]and that is [G]just the reason
[D7]I tell it [G]now to thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]I love to tell the story;
[C]'tis pleasant [G]to repeat
[D]what seems, each [G]time I tell it,
[D]more wonderfully sweet.
[D7]I love to [G]tell the story,
[Em]for some [B]have never heard
[C]the message [G]of salvation
[D7]from God's [G]own holy Word.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]I love to tell the story,
[C]for those who [G]know it best
[D]seem hungering [G]and thirsting
[D]to hear it like the rest.
[D7]And when, in [G]scenes of glory,
[Em]I sing the [B]new, new song,
[C]'twill be the [G]old, old story
[D7]that I have [G]loved so long.
{end_of_verse}
